      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A stock notice and the request list are visible near the lending station.\", \"decision\": \"How should the café explain a temporary cup shortage?\", \"goal\": \"Make cup lending and return convenient while keeping the available stock and volunteer work understandable.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood café wants to lend reusable cups at community gatherings and recover them afterward. It has a modest cup stock, washable collection crates, a simple lending record, and volunteers who can share short shifts. The plan concerns a small pilot with no deposit or sales system. Different decisions address separate moments in lending, return, and review.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nOne volunteer updates the stock notice while another works through the request list. Shared information and individual arrangements proceed together.\nVolunteers speak with guests on the request list first and then put the agreed options on the stock notice. The shared message reflects the choices already offered to waiting guests.\nVolunteers update the stock notice first and then explain the next options to guests on the request list. All guests see the shortage before individual arrangements are discussed."
    }
